  "findings": [
    "Four additional access maps use two separate WGFD-listed Gas Wells public access areas on the Green and New Fork rivers.",
    "Four complete trial courses were rejected because source geometry crosses old channels or vegetated islands; access maps can remain useful without those paths.",
    "Lower Hoback unresolved sites now carry the actual Forest Service launch restriction. No private ranch permission or designated ramp inferred.",
    "Stoney Point remains held because its agency coordinate appears to duplicate the already-corrected Dubois park vicinity; a town park listing does not resolve that identity conflict."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Local only; no publication.",
    "Gas Wells markers are approximate access areas, not exact rebuilt ramps or bank-side instructions.",
    "No existing verified coordinate, stable access ID, planning mile, gauge, calibration or GPS remaining-time setting was changed."
  ],
